# NGO Volunteer Management Portal
## User Flow Document

**Key decisions applied in this version:**
- NGOs can publish events **immediately** after signup (no admin pre-approval gate)
- Volunteer search uses **geo-radius (10km) filtering**, not just exact pincode match
- **No in-app chat** — NGO and Volunteer contact each other via **visible email/phone**
- Admin role exists in background only for moderation/reporting, not as a publishing gate

---

## 1. Landing Page Flow

```
Landing Page
 ├── "I'm an NGO" → NGO Sign Up
 ├── "I'm a Volunteer" → Volunteer Sign Up
 ├── "Browse Events" (public, read-only preview, no filters by location until signed in/pincode entered)
 └── Login (role auto-detected from account)
```

---

## 2. NGO Flow

### 2.1 NGO Registration

```
Click "Register as NGO"
   │
   ▼
Sign Up Form
 - Org Name, Official Email, Phone, Password
 - Registration/Trust Number
 - Upload Registration Certificate (PDF/Image) — stored, shown as "Verification: Pending" badge
   │
   ▼
Email OTP Verification
   │
   ▼
NGO Dashboard unlocked immediately
 (badge shows "Unverified" until admin reviews docs in background;
  NGO can publish events right away regardless of badge status)
```

> Verification badge is informational/trust-building for volunteers, not a publishing gate. Admin can revoke/suspend an NGO later if docs turn out fraudulent — but that's a moderation flow, separate from the happy path.

### 2.2 Create Event Flow

```
NGO Dashboard → "Create New Event"
   │
   ▼
Event Form
 - Title, Description, Category
 - Date/Time, Duration
 - Address + Pincode (auto-geocoded to lat/lng in background)
 - Total volunteers needed + role-wise breakdown (e.g. 5 teaching, 3 logistics)
 - Banner image
 - Contact for this event: email + phone (auto-filled from org profile, editable)
   │
   ▼
Click "Publish" → Event goes LIVE immediately, instantly searchable
```

### 2.3 Managing Applications

```
NGO Dashboard → Event → Applicants Tab
   │
   ▼
List of volunteer applicants (name, skills, distance from event, contact email/phone visible)
   │
   ├── Accept → Volunteer notified, slot count decreases
   ├── Reject → Volunteer notified
   └── Waitlist → auto-promoted if accepted volunteer cancels
   │
   ▼
Event Day: Mark Attendance (per volunteer)
   │
   ▼
Issue Certificate (auto-generated PDF, downloadable by volunteer)
```

### 2.4 NGO Dashboard Map

```
NGO Dashboard
 ├── Overview (active events, total applicants, upcoming events)
 ├── My Events (Create / Edit / Cancel / Duplicate)
 ├── Applications (per event: pending / accepted / rejected / waitlisted)
 ├── Org Profile (logo, about, causes, registration docs, contact info)
 ├── Verification Status (read-only, shows pending/verified/rejected)
 └── Notifications (new applications, cancellations)
```

---

## 3. Volunteer Flow

### 3.1 Volunteer Registration

```
Click "Join as Volunteer"
   │
   ▼
Sign Up Form
 - Name, Email, Phone, Password
 - Pincode (geocoded to lat/lng for radius search)
 - Skills/Interests (multi-select)
 - Availability (weekday/weekend/full-time)
   │
   ▼
Email OTP Verification
   │
   ▼
Volunteer Dashboard unlocked
```

### 3.2 Discover & Apply Flow

```
Volunteer Dashboard → "Discover Events"
   │
   ▼
Default view: events within 10km of volunteer's saved pincode
   │
   ▼
Filters available:
 - Radius slider (e.g. 5km / 10km / 25km / 50km / custom)
 - Category/Cause
 - Date range
 - Skill required
 - Spots remaining (urgency)
 - NGO name search
   │
   ▼
List View ←→ Map View toggle
   │
   ▼
Click Event → Event Detail Page
 - Full description, NGO profile, location map, spots filled (e.g. 12/20)
 - NGO contact email + phone displayed directly on page
   │
   ▼
Click "Apply"
 - Optional short message to NGO
   │
   ▼
Application submitted → status "Pending"
   │
   ▼
NGO accepts/rejects → Volunteer notified (email + in-app notification)
   │
   ▼
If accepted: volunteer can contact NGO directly via shown email/phone for coordination
```

### 3.3 Volunteer Dashboard Map

```
Volunteer Dashboard
 ├── Discover Events (filters incl. 10km radius default)
 ├── My Applications (pending / accepted / rejected / completed)
 ├── My Impact (hours volunteered, events completed, certificates)
 ├── Profile (skills, pincode, availability)
 └── Notifications (status updates, new matching events nearby)
```

---

## 4. End-to-End Loop (Combined View)

```
NGO publishes event (live instantly, geocoded location)
        │
        ▼
Volunteer searches within 10km radius of their pincode
        │
        ▼
Volunteer applies (with optional message)
        │
        ▼
NGO sees applicant + their contact email/phone, accepts/rejects
        │
        ▼
Volunteer notified; if accepted, both parties coordinate directly via email/phone
        │
        ▼
Event happens → NGO marks attendance
        │
        ▼
Certificate issued → Volunteer's impact stats updated
```

---

## 5. Notification Triggers (Both Sides)

| Trigger | Notify |
|---|---|
| New volunteer application | NGO |
| Application accepted/rejected/waitlisted | Volunteer |
| Event nearing date (reminder) | Both |
| New event published within volunteer's 10km radius matching their skills | Volunteer |
| Volunteer cancels application | NGO |
| Certificate issued | Volunteer |